  "body": {
    "id": "thm:universal-airy-law",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Theorem 1. On the explicit union \\[\\{(2,(1,-1)),(2,(-1,1))\\}\\cup\\{(K,c):K\\ge3,\\ c\\in\\mathcal C_K\\},\\] the unrestricted risk satisfies \\[R_n(c)=n^{-1}-C_AV_c(s_c/2)^{2/3}n^{-4/3}+o(n^{-4/3}),\\qquad \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}d_n(c)=\\Lambda_c.\\] On the at-least-three-active-arm component, the independent allocation \\(q^\\star\\) and the total full-label nonlinear Airy estimator attain the expansion. On the published two-arm component, the two-arm reduction proposition gives \\(V_c(s_c/2)=1\\) and recovers Sudijono, Dobriban, and Tchetgen Tchetgen (2026), Theorem 3.1. Thus the union contains the published two-arm class as its first component and adds every fixed normalized contrast with at least three active arms as its second component, with the two-arm reduction providing the bridge.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "K",
      "c",
      "\\mathcal C_K",
      "R_n(c)",
      "n",
      "C_A",
      "V_c",
      "s_c",
      "d_n(c)",
      "\\Lambda_c",
      "q^\\star",
      "\\delta_n^\\star"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:contrast-class",
